.TH tkutoolbar n 0.2 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkutoolbar
.PP
A toolbar holding buttons, toggles, dropdowns, separators and arbitrary embedded widgets, addressed by caller\-chosen ids. Theme\-native (built\-in \fBToolbutton\fR style, dark\-theme safe). Pure Tk. The 0.1 positional API is a strict subset, so old callers keep working unchanged.
.SS Construct
.CS
set tb [::tkutils::tkutoolbar::widget .tb \
    ?-orient horizontal|vertical? ?-displaymode icon|text|both? \
    ?-spacing px? ?-padding px? ?-buttonstyle flat|raised?]
.CE
.PP
\fB\-buttonstyle flat\fR (default) uses the flat \fBToolbutton\fR style (button edges show on hover); \fB\-buttonstyle raised\fR gives push buttons and dropdowns a visible border (\fBTButton\fR/\fBTMenubutton\fR), so it is obvious where each button begins. Toggles keep the flat pressed\-state look in both modes.
.SS Items
.CS
::tkutils::tkutoolbar::addButton   $tb id label command \
    ?-icon img? ?-tooltip s? ?-shortcut key? ?-compound side? \
    ?-displaymode m? ?-side left|right? ?ttk::button opts...?
::tkutils::tkutoolbar::addToggle   $tb id label varName \
    ?-icon img? ?-tooltip s? ?-command cmd? ?-onvalue v? ?-offvalue v? ?...?
::tkutils::tkutoolbar::addDropdown $tb id label \
    ?-icon img? ?-tooltip s? ?-menu {{label cmd} - {label cmd} ...}?
::tkutils::tkutoolbar::addSeparator $tb
::tkutils::tkutoolbar::addWidget    $tb id childWidget ?side?   ;# embed your own
.CE
.PP
\fBlabel\fR/\fBcommand\fR stay positional for \fBaddButton\fR/\fBaddToggle\fR; any further \fB\-option value\fR pairs are recognised (the toolbar options above) or forwarded to the underlying ttk widget. \fB\-shortcut\fR binds on the toplevel and is released automatically when the toolbar is destroyed.
.SS "Mutate / query"
.CS
::tkutils::tkutoolbar::setEnabled      $tb id 0|1
::tkutils::tkutoolbar::configureButton $tb id ?-option value ...?
::tkutils::tkutoolbar::setCallback     $tb id command
::tkutils::tkutoolbar::setDisplayMode  $tb icon|text|both     ;# whole toolbar
::tkutils::tkutoolbar::getDisplayMode  $tb
::tkutils::tkutoolbar::buttonWidget    $tb id                 ;# the widget path
::tkutils::tkutoolbar::items           $tb                    ;# ids in order
.CE
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
Tooltips are delegated to \fBtkutils::tkuballoon\fR (a runtime dependency).
.IP \(bu
\fBicon\fR mode without an \fB\-icon\fR falls back to text; \fBboth\fR uses \fB\-compound\fR.
.IP \(bu
Errors carry \fB{TKUTILS TKUTOOLBAR <REASON>}\fR (\fBOPTION\fR, \fBORIENT\fR, \fBDISPLAYMODE\fR, \fBBUTTONSTYLE\fR, \fBNOITEM\fR, \fBNOTOOLBAR\fR).
.SS "Launcher / demos"
.CS
tclsh bin/tkutoolbar.tcl
tclsh examples/demo-tkutoolbar.tcl          # text buttons, display modes
tclsh examples/demo-tkutoolbar-icons.tcl    # icons (via tkuicon) + flat vs raised
.CE
.SS "Additional exported commands"
.PP
Documented for completeness (same module, also covered by the test suite):
.CS
tkutoolbar::addAction path name ?id?           ;# add a toolbar button bound to a tkuaction id (enabled/checked state follows the action)
.CE
